UnitMetaquoter::QuoteAddClLiquidityV3
├── when the pool is not a registered target
│   └── it reverts with IP
└── given the pool is a registered target
    ├── when the target factory is not approved
    │   └── it reverts with AF
    └── given the target factory is approved
        ├── when the pool type is not CL
        │   └── it reverts with PT
        └── given the pool type is CL
            ├── when the lower tick is not below the upper tick
            │   └── it reverts with TLU
            ├── when the lower tick is below the minimum tick
            │   └── it reverts with TLM
            ├── when the upper tick is above the maximum tick
            │   └── it reverts with TUM
            ├── when the lower tick is not aligned to the tick spacing
            │   └── it reverts with TS
            ├── when the upper tick is not aligned to the tick spacing
            │   └── it reverts with TS
            └── given the tick range is valid
                ├── when one desired side is zero inside the range
                │   └── it reverts with ILM
                ├── when the desired amounts size liquidity above the int128 maximum
                │   └── it reverts with LTM
                ├── when the price is inside the range
                │   ├── it returns the liquidity the position manager would mint
                │   └── it returns both amounts rounded up at the live price
                ├── when the amounts are compared to the burn valuation
                │   └── it returns amounts at most one wei above the rounded down ones
                ├── when the price is below the range
                │   ├── it sizes the liquidity from amount0Desired alone
                │   └── it returns zero as amount1
                ├── when the price is above the range
                │   ├── it sizes the liquidity from amount1Desired alone
                │   └── it returns zero as amount0
                ├── when the unbounded side is the maximum uint256 below the range
                │   └── it quotes the bounded side alone
                ├── when the unbounded side is the maximum uint256 inside the range
                │   └── it reverts without a reason
                ├── when the price sits at the upper tick ratio with the tick one below
                │   └── it returns zero as amount0
                ├── when the tick is the lower tick with the price inside it
                │   ├── it returns both amounts rounded up at the live price
                │   └── it returns both sides nonzero
                ├── when the tick is the upper tick with the price inside it
                │   └── it returns zero as amount0
                └── when the quote is taken at a pinned price and range
                    └── it returns the amounts the mint callback would pull
